UID:s0CV4DgjBRkUhV15K1oEA
SUMMARY:HXD Week: "Beyond the Lease" Panel Discusion + PDR Office Tour
DTSTAMP:20260804T053520Z
DTSTART:20260804T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the Lease: Why Employees Chose Places Not Offices + PDR 
	Tour\nJoin us for a panel discussion exploring how development priorities 
	have evolved\, what today’s tenants expect\, and how creating an experienc
	e-driven workplace can influence leasing decisions\, company culture\, and
	 employee attraction and retention. \nModerator \nMarc Bellamy\, RA\, NCAR
	B\, Fitwel Ambassador\nPrincipal + Owner\nPDR \nMarc is a Principal and Ow
	ner at PDR with 25 years of experience in corporate interiors\, base build
	ing design and real estate development. Throughout his time with PDR\, Mar
	c has worked on numerous projects for ExxonMobil\, Jefferies Group\, Vitol
	\, and many other varied clients\, coordinating ongoing work and deliverin
	g high-performance workplace solutions. \n  \nPanelists \nJohn Connett\nSe
	nior Director\nCushman & Wakefield \nI am a commercial real estate and con
	struction management executive with 30 years of end-to-end industry experi
	ence\, progressing from hands-on field craftsmanship to leading market ope
	rations for a global real estate leader. As Senior Director and Market Lea
	d at Cushman & Wakefield\, I specialize in scaling business units\, buildi
	ng elite project teams\, and protecting client capital across multi-millio
	n-dollar portfolios. Whether directing a high-end downtown interior buildo
	ut\, managing an industrial hub\, or aligning capital market strategies\, 
	I combine a macro-level real estate vision with a common-sense approach to
	 execution. I thrive at the intersection of aggressive market expansion an
	d disciplined financial containment – consistently delivering top-line gro
	wth and maximizing operational efficiency. \n  \nPhilip Croker\nSenior Man
	aging Direct\nRockefeller Group Houston \nPhilip Croker leads Rockefeller 
	Group’s Southwest Region\, overseeing acquisitions\, development\, and ope
	rations across Texas and Arizona. With more than two decades of experience
	 in commercial real estate development\, he has led many of Houston’s most
	 significant office projects and brings a developer’s perspective on creat
	ing workplaces that attract today’s tenants. \n  \nBrian Gabbard\, RID\nDe
	sign Director\nPDR \nBrian Gabbard is the Design Director for PDR – based 
	in the Houston office. With over 25 years of award-winning design experien
	ce across the U.S. and internationally\, he is known for his client-focuse
	d approach and ability to create transformative environments that positive
	ly impact users and occupants. As a natural storyteller\, Brian develops d
	esign solutions built around a narrative unique to each client and project
	 and brings a thoughtful perspective and immersive approach to every space
	 that he helps to shape. Drawing inspiration from his multicultural backgr
	ound and global travels\, he pulls from multiple influences to craft sophi
	sticated and impactful design solutions. \n  \nMark Reilly\nJLL\nVice Pres
	ident \nMark Reilly is a Vice President with JLL’s Houston occupier adviso
	ry team\, representing corporate clients in office and industrial real est
	ate strategy. His work spans portfolio optimization\, tenant representatio
	n\, and workplace decision-making\, helping organizations align their real
	 estate with changing business and employee expectations. \n  \n  \nLight 
	bites and beverages will be provided. \nParking: Free surface lot and stre
	et parking available. Parking is limited\, rideshare encouraged.\n\nhttps:
	//architecturehouston.org/event/pdrtour/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/pdrtour/
LOCATION:Private: PDR\, 927 Studewood St.\, Floor 2\, Houston\, TX\, 77008\
	, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
